    <name>
      <text>Proving a Difference Quotient</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p> If \(f(x)={@fx@}\), show that </p>
<p>\( \qquad \quad \displaystyle {@fx@} \left(\frac{{@constant^(h)@}-1}{h} \right )=\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\)</p>
<p>Proof Steps:</p>

<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Let's begin from the <strong>R.H.S. </strong>Calculate \(f(x+h)\) using \(f(x)\):</p>
<p>\(\qquad \quad  f(x) = {@fx@}\)</p>
<p>\(\qquad \quad  f(x+h) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] \( \ldots \bigstar\)</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><strong>Step \(2\):</strong> Rewrite \(\bigstar\) in the form \(a^m \cdot a^n\) using exponent properties:</p>
<p>\(\qquad  \quad f(x+h) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p><strong>Step \(3\):</strong> Subtract \(f(x)\) from \(f(x+h)\):</p>
<p>\(\qquad  \quad f(x+h) - f(x)  = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p><strong>Step \(4\):</strong> Divide both sides by \(h\) and recognize the left side as the derivative of \(f(x)\) with respect to \(x\), denoted as \(f'(x)\)</p>
<div style="text-align: left; margin-left: 1cm;">
<p>So, [[input:ans4]][[validation:ans4]] </p>
<p> [[feedback:prt4]] </p>
</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p> If \(f(x)={@fx@}\), show that </p>
<p>\( \qquad \quad \displaystyle {@fx@} \left(\frac{{@constant^(h)@}-1}{h} \right )=\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\)</p>
<p>Proof Steps:</p>

<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Let's begin from the <strong>R.H.S. </strong>Calculate \(f(x+h)\) using \(f(x)\):</p>
<p>\(\qquad \quad  f(x) = {@fx@}\)</p>
<p>\(\qquad \quad  f(x+h) = {@fxh@} \ldots \bigstar\)</p>

<p><strong>Step \(2\):</strong> Rewrite \(\bigstar\) in the form \(a^m \cdot a^n\) using exponent properties:</p>
<p>\(\qquad  \quad f(x+h) = {@constant^(x)@} \cdot {@constant^(h)@}\)</p>

<p><strong>Step \(3\):</strong> Subtract \(f(x)\) from \(f(x+h)\):</p>
<p>\(\qquad  \quad \begin{align} 
 f(x+h) - f(x)  &= {@fx_lhs@} \\
                       &= \left({@constant^(x)@} \cdot {@constant^(h)@} \right)-{@fx@} \\
                                        &= {@fx_factored@} 
\end{align} \)</p>

<p><strong>Step \(4\):</strong> Divide both sides by \(h\) and recognize the left side as the derivative of \(f(x)\) with respect to \(x\), denoted as \(f'(x)\):</p>
<p>\(\qquad \quad  \displaystyle \frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h} =  {@fx@} \left(\frac{{@constant^(h)@}-1}{h} \right )\)</p>

<p>So, \( \displaystyle \frac{{@fx_factored@} }{h} = {@fx@} \left(\frac{{@constant^(h)@}-1}{h} \right )=\textbf{L.H.S}\), proving the given equation.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
